| SIB (Static Initialization Block)         | IIB (Instance Initialization Block)  |
| ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| `static { }`                              | `{ }`                                |
| Runs only once when the class is loaded   | Runs every time an object is created |
| Used for class-level initialization       | Used for object-level initialization |
| Cannot directly access instance variables | Can access instance variables        |
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SIB (Static Initialization Block) = "Runs once for the class."
IIB (Instance Initialization Block) = "Runs once for every object."


| Concept               | Example               | Purpose                                                                              |
| --------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **SIB**               | `static { }`          | Runs **once** when the class is loaded.                                              |
| **IIB**               | `{ }`                 | Runs **every time** an object is created, before the constructor.                    |
| **`this`**            | `this.name = name;`   | Refers to the current object's variables or calls another constructor with `this()`. |
| **`super`**           | `super("Bangalore");` | Calls the parent class constructor or accesses parent members.                       |
| **Constructor**       | `SBIUser(...)`        | Initializes the object when it is created.                                           |
| **Method**            | `display()`           | Performs an action using the object's data.                                          |
| **Static Variable**   | `objectCount`         | One shared copy for the entire class.                                                |
| **Instance Variable** | `name`, `balance`     | Each object has its own copy.                                                        |



